[2026-05-26 12:57:25] [claude-sdk] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is working through Issue #194 in the SLANG compiler: closing \"backend feature gaps\" in the oscar_c (Commodore 64 / oscar64) backend for ARRAY InitialCode emit support. This follows PR #193 (Issue #190) which moved ARRAY validation to SemanticAnalyzer. The approach is \"1 PR = 1 gap\" with user choosing each gap target. Four PRs were created in this session:\n   - PR #195: ARRAY WORD InitialCode emit (merged)\n   - PR #196: StringLiteral in ARRAY BYTE InitialCode (merged)\n   - PR #197: CodeLabelRef / non-const element diagnosis as permanent oscar64 constraint (merged)\n   - User's latest message: \"マージしました。メインに戻ってください。\" = merged PR #197, return to main\n\n   Security/operational constraints (must persist):\n   - \"commit 後の自動 push / PR 作成は確認を取る\" (confirm before auto push/PR after commit)\n   - \"working tree 変更を勝手に revert しない\" (don't unilaterally revert working tree)\n   - \"license 関連 docs は事前 review 必須\" (license docs need pre-review)\n   - \"CHANGELOG / commit docs は確定事項のみ\" (commit docs: confirmed facts only)\n   - oscar64 is GPL-3.0-only, SLANG is MIT - never borrow GPL source, only #include headers\n   - \"個人情報 (メアド等) はテキスト化しない\"\n   - \"GitHub Release は Pre-release\" (`gh release create` には `--prerelease` を必ず付ける)\n   - SLANG ARRAY[N] = 要素数 N+1 (memory feedback)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - SLANG `= { ... }` is CODE byte stream, not array element initializer\n   - `BuildArrayInitFromCode` returns `ArrayInitEmitResult(InitText, SourceByteCount, EmittedByteCount, CElementCount, IsCStringLiteral)` record\n   - BYTE path: hex literals `{0xNN, ...}`, CElementCount = SourceByteCount\n   - WORD path: byte stream → 2-byte LE grouping → `{0xNNNN, ...}`, CElementCount = EmittedByteCount/2, odd bytes get 0-padding\n   - StringLiteral path: C string literal `\"hello\"` emit (not hex), oscar64 `-psci` for PETSCII auto-conversion, CElementCount = char len + 1 (NUL)\n   - Non-const address references (Function/Array) in static `unsigned int[]` initializers are **permanently rejected** by oscar64 (error 3008), though `void*[]` / `void(*[])(void)` work\n   - `_unsizedArraysWithInit` HashSet tracks global unsized+InitialCode symbols for assignment rejection, `_scope.IsLocal()` gating prevents shadowing false positives\n   - C implicit zero fill for underfilled fixed arrays (not helper-side fill)\n   - SLANG lexer escape semantics: `\\n`→CR(0x0D), `\\r`→0x1c, `\\t`→'t' literal, `\\0`→'0' literal\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`src/SLANGCompiler.Core/CodeGen/C/CEmitter.cs`** (primary modification target)\n     - `ArrayInitEmitResult` record (around L416): `private sealed record ArrayInitEmitResult(string InitText, int SourceByteCount, int EmittedByteCount, int CElementCount, bool IsCStringLiteral = false);`\n     - `BuildArrayInitFromCode` (L430-580 area): Main helper with 3 short-circuit paths (StringLiteral single, WORD-only was added then removed for 3b) + byte stream loop with BYTE/WORD output formatting\n     - StringLiteral path: ASCII printable (0x20-0x7E) + CR (0x0D, SLANG `\\n`) only whitelist; non-ASCII/NUL/control chars rejected\n     - Non-const IdentifierExpr path: Function/MachineFunction/ARRAY global symbols get specific oscar64 error 3008 message with runtime init workaround hint; others get generic non-const error\n     - Fixed-path callers (global L392, static L702): `IsCStringLiteral && CElementCount > totalSize` NUL fit check\n     - Unsized-path callers (global L328, static L659): use `CElementCount` for C array dimension\n     - `_unsizedArraysWithInit` tracking: global-scope only (EmitStaticDecl removed its Add), VisitAssignExpr gated by `!_scope.IsLocal(tid.Name)`\n   \n   - **`tests/SLANGCompiler.Tests/ArrayInitOscarCTests.cs`** (test file, heavily extended)\n     - 71+ tests total covering BYTE, WORD, StringLiteral, and permanent reject cases\n     - WORD tests: AllWordValues, DefaultByteItems grouped LE, OddByteCount padding, Underfilled implicit fill, UnsizedCElementCount, UnsizedOddByte, UnsizedAssignment reject, LocalStatic\n     - StringLiteral tests: UnsizedSingle, FixedExact, FixedUnderfill, FixedOverflow semantic, MixedReject, WORDReject, LocalStatic, EscapeQuoteBackslash, AllowedNewline, NulReject, NonAsciiReject, ControlCharReject, FixedNulFit reject (global + local)\n     - Label ref tests: FunctionRef reject, ArrayRef reject, ScalarGlobalVar reject, ArrayByte_FunctionRef reject (renamed from LabelRef)\n   \n   - **`CHANGELOG.md`**: Updated with entries for WORD init, StringLiteral init, and permanent address-ref backend gap\n   \n   - **`src/SLANGCompiler.Core/CodeGen/C/CStringEncoder.cs`**: Existing helper, Encode() outputs C string literal with escape sequences. Known limitation: `\\0` + octal digit eating (NUL now rejected in ARRAY init path)\n   \n   - **Issue #194**: Created to track 5 oscar_c backend gaps; (1a) WORD, (3a) StringLiteral, (3b) CodeLabelRef all addressed\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Build cache**: `dotnet $SLANGC` picked up stale dll after edit, force rebuild with `--no-incremental` needed multiple times\n   - **CS0136 variable name collision**: StringLiteral path locals `cElementCount`/`initText` collided with enclosing scope → renamed to `strCElementCount`/`strInitText`/`strSourceBytes`\n   - **SLANG `\\n` = CR not LF**: Test expected `\"hi\\n\"` → C `\"hi\\n\"` but SLANG lexer converts `\\n` to CR (0x0D), so C output is `\"hi\\r\"` → fixed test expectation\n   - **oscar64 error 3008**: Static `unsigned int[]` initializer with `(unsigned int)F_FUNC` / `(unsigned int)V_BUF` fails in oscar64. User confirmed via local oscar64 testing. Resolution: permanent backend gap with runtime init workaround message\n   - **NUL + octal digit C escape**: CStringEncoder outputs `\\0` for NUL, but C interprets `\\07` as octal 7 not NUL+'7'. Resolution: NUL removed from whitelist\n   - **Workaround message incomplete**: Unsized `ARRAY WORD JT[]` without InitialCode becomes pointer decl in oscar_c, so workaround must mention fixed-size declaration → message updated\n   - **Test name mismatch**: `ArrayByte_LabelRef_*` was actually testing `%FUNC1` (CastExpr+IdentifierExpr), not CodeLabelRef (`<LABEL>`) → renamed to `ArrayByte_FunctionRef_*`\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - ARRAY WORD InitialCode: Solved by byte stream → 2-byte LE WORD literal grouping, with ArrayInitEmitResult record to separate byte count from C element count\n   - StringLiteral: Solved by C string literal emit (oscar64 `-psci` PETSCII) with ASCII printable + CR whitelist, NUL fit check for fixed arrays\n   - Address references: Discovered oscar64 doesn't support address-to-integer cast in static init; pivoted from emit support to permanent reject with informative error messages and workaround guidance\n   - Shadowing fix (from context start): `_scope.IsLocal()` gating prevents global `_unsizedArraysWithInit` from falsely rejecting local variable assignments\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Context start) Codex review Medium about CEmitter L1332 checking only IsArrayDecl\n   - \"ありがとうございます。マージしました。mainに戻り、プランとissueを確認して次の対応を検討してください。\"\n   - Selected \"v3 完了整理 + v3b-E issue 化\" for next step\n   - \"Issue #194の設計をお願いします。\" (entered plan mode)\n   - Selected \"(1a) ARRAY WORD InitialCode\" as first PR gap\n   - Plan mode Codex review feedback (4 findings: High unsized byteCount, Medium capacity fill, Medium byteCount semantics, Low error messages)\n   - Plan approved\n   - Selected \"はい、 push + PR 作成\" for PR #195\n   - \"レビュー問題なしです。マージしました。次に進みましょう。\"\n   - Selected \"(3a) StringLiteral in ARRAY BYTE (Recommended)\" as next gap\n   - Selected \"(A) StringLiteral 単独のみ対応\" for mixed scope\n   - Selected \"(A2) unsized + 固定サイズ両方\